  Two Aetheria packages were assessed and deliberately NOT ported:

  `packages/memory/` — `src/cognition/memory/` already implements a strictly
  stronger durable memory store (revision-checked batches, secret scanning,
  byte budgets, per-session snapshots) on `node:sqlite`. Porting Aetheria's
  simpler per-user turn/fact table would have added a second, weaker memory
  system rather than a capability.

  `packages/channel-telegram/` — `src/telegram/runner.ts` is ARI OS's own
  chain-agnostic long-poll runner over `src/gateway/channels/`. Adopting the
  grammY bot would have added a production dependency and a second Telegram
  implementation to reach the same API.

  `packages/mcp/src/json-schema.ts` was likewise not ported: it is a
  hand-rolled zod→JSON-Schema shim, and ARI OS already depends on
  `zod-to-json-schema`, whose output `ToolRegistry.schemas()` emits.

  src/chains/solana/spl.ts is NOT derived from Aetheria and is not covered by
  Apache-2.0. It is a clean-room MIT file written for ARI OS to replace the
  `@solana/spl-token` dependency: three public on-chain program addresses and
  one instruction built from the Associated Token Account program's documented
  wire format. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. tests/solana-spl.test.ts is likewise
  new and MIT.

