Modifications made (Apache-2.0 §4(b))
─────────────────────────────────────

  * `@aetheria/*` package specifiers replaced with relative ESM imports; the
    pnpm workspace layout is flattened into ARI OS's single-package `src/`.
  * `src/kernel/store.ts` — the SQLite driver is `node:sqlite`'s `DatabaseSync`
    (ARI OS's house primitive) instead of better-sqlite3, and the reserve
    transaction is an explicit BEGIN IMMEDIATE / COMMIT / ROLLBACK block
    instead of better-sqlite3's `db.transaction()` helper. Schema, cap
    semantics and the single-writer guarantee are unchanged.
  * `src/kernel/selfcheck/run.ts` — returns a structured report instead of only
    printing, so the invariants run both as a script and under vitest.
  * `src/kernel/contracts.ts` — the Aetheria `shared` package is consolidated
    into one module; the LLM, tool-registry, Telegram-runtime, env-config and
    market-data contracts are deliberately not carried over (ARI OS has its
    own). Doc comments referring to Aetheria-specific commands are reworded.
  * `src/kernel/lock.ts`, `src/kernel/policy-engine.ts` — user-facing error text
    rebranded from Aetheria to ARI OS; behaviour unchanged.
  * `src/chains/solana/rpc.ts` — the constructor also accepts an existing
    `Connection` so the read ports can be exercised without a live RPC.
  * `src/kernel/contracts.ts` — `IntentKind` widened from the literal `'swap'`
    to the four perp kinds and the eight pool/curve kinds; `TradeIntent` gained
    an optional `perp` leg; the `PositionReader` port and `SettleMode` were
    added. The Aetheria `shared` tool contract (`ToolContext`, `Preview`,
    `ToolDefinition`) IS now carried over after all, since `src/perps` and
    `src/pools` are written against it — renamed to `IntentToolDefinition` /
    `ToolOutcome` so it does not collide with ARI OS's own registry contract in
    `src/agent/types.ts`.
  * `src/kernel/policy-engine.ts` — the "input amount must be positive" rule is
    gated on the intent kind so a perp reduce/close (which posts no collateral)
    is not refused, and the bps-of-notional priority-fee ceiling is skipped when
    the input leg is zero for the same reason. Every other guard is unchanged.
  * `src/kernel/trade-gateway.ts` — added the `venue-position` settle branch:
    perp kinds are verified against the venue position delta rather than a token
    balance delta, and a perp intent with no `PositionReader` mounted is refused
    before broadcast.
  * `src/perps/intent.ts` — the `IntentKind` cast in `asTradeIntent` is gone
    (the widened kernel types make it unnecessary), and the doc comment that
    described the missing perp settle now describes the implemented one.
  * `src/pools/intent.ts` — pool intents declare their real kind (`lp_open`,
    `curve_buy`, …) instead of flattening to `'swap'`.
  * `src/perps/*`, `src/pools/*` — `node:test` replaced with vitest in the
    ported tests, which moved from co-located `*.test.ts` into `tests/`;
    optional interface properties widened to `?: T | undefined` where ARI OS's
    `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` requires it; three latent unused-binding lint
    errors fixed.
  * `@drift-labs/sdk`, `@meteora-ag/dlmm` and `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` are
    declared as OPTIONAL peer dependencies rather than dependencies, so they
    stay out of the lockfile and out of `npm audit --omit=dev`; the lazy
    loaders' error text names the npm install command.
  * `src/data/pumpportal.ts` — the `ws` package is replaced by Node's built-in
    global `WebSocket` (WHATWG, stable in Node 22), so the keyless PumpPortal
    feed adds no production dependency. That API has no `terminate()` or
    `removeAllListeners()`, so a monotonic socket generation makes a superseded
    socket's late frames inert instead; the reconnect and watchdog timers are
    `unref`'d so a market feed never holds the process open; and a frame whose
    size does not parse as a finite non-negative number is dropped rather than
    admitted as `NaN`.
  * `src/data/signals-engine.ts` — the `RugHeat` interface is imported from
    `src/pools/signals.ts` (where ARI OS extracted it) rather than redeclared,
    and the class states `implements RugHeatSource`, so satisfying the port the
    pools guards read is checked by the compiler. Scoring is unchanged.
  * `src/data/feed.ts` — NEW. Aetheria wired tape + watcher + engine inside its
    engine package, which ARI OS does not have. `SignalsFeed` is that wiring
    with a lifecycle the composition root owns: the engine exists from
    construction (so `guardRugHeat` always has a source) while `start()` — the
    network side effect — belongs to `Application.start()`. Auto-following new
    launches is bounded, and explicitly watched mints are pinned against
    eviction.
  * `src/strategy/store.ts` — `node:sqlite`'s `DatabaseSync` instead of
    better-sqlite3; `.changes` is read through `Number()` because `node:sqlite`
    returns it as a bigint; `setStatus` returns whether a row was hit so the
    console can answer 404; an unparseable `params` blob degrades to `{}`
    rather than throwing inside the tick loop; `all()` was added for the
    console, which shows every strategy rather than one user's.
  * `src/strategy/runner.ts` — Aetheria's `SwapRequest` came from its `shared`
    runtime contract, which ARI OS deliberately did not carry over, so the
    request shape is declared locally as `StrategySwap`; the tick timer is
    `unref`'d. The planning logic, the error breaker and the reschedule
    arithmetic are unchanged.
  * `src/strategy/executor.ts` — NEW, and the reason the port is honest.
    Aetheria's runner called an engine-level `swap()` that owned quoting and
    execution. ARI OS has no such engine, so `gatewayExecutor` quotes through
    `JupiterClient`, assembles a plain `TradeIntent` and hands it to
    `TradeGateway.execute()` — the same chokepoint every tool uses. It holds no
    keypair, no broadcaster and no RPC write. `confirmedByUser` is never set:
    an unattended schedule cannot assert that a human confirmed a trade, so an
    unpinned mint is refused by `MINT_NOT_PINNED` rather than waved through.
  * `src/strategy/view.ts` — NEW. Aetheria surfaced strategies as Telegram
    text; ARI OS has a console, so this projects a row onto its `StrategyView`,
    following `src/control/snapshot.ts`'s rule of never inventing a number (no
    trigger without a real price reading, no budget meter without a budget).
  * `src/mcp/server.ts` — the tool set is ARI OS's `ToolRegistry` rather than
    Aetheria's `AnyTool[]`, so the handler delegates to `registry.invoke()`
    (which already owns validation, capability checks, timeouts and the audit
    event) instead of re-validating and calling `tool.execute()` itself. The
    granted capability set comes from the composition root and cannot be
    widened by a request; a tool outside it is not listed at all.
  * `src/bin/mcp.ts` — Aetheria's bin threw on every `tools/call` because it
    had no way to build a tool context. ARI OS composes the same `Application`
    the daemon does, mounts no custody, and grants read-only capabilities.
  * Source formatting normalised to ARI OS's Prettier configuration.
